@startuml
hide footbox
title UC-06 Select a Corgi class during character creation
actor Player
participant "Frontend\n(Character creation)" as FE
participant "Backend\n(Character service)" as BE
database "SQLite\n(Characters/classes)" as DB

Player -> FE : Start creating new Corgi
FE -> BE : Request three starter class definitions
BE -> DB : Read Barkmage, S.P.A.W. Agent, Barkguard
DB --> BE : Class definitions / milestone previews
BE --> FE : Available classes and starting features
FE --> Player : Show 3 classes and base Corgi abilities

Player -> FE : Choose class; review class preview
FE --> Player : Show starting / future class features
Player -> FE : Confirm character creation and class
FE -> BE : Create character (details, classId)
BE -> DB : Validate class and insert new character
with class and initial progression (transaction)
alt Valid request and transaction succeeds
    DB --> BE : Character persisted (id, classId)
    BE --> FE : Creation successful; roster updated
    FE --> Player : Confirm new Corgi and selected class
else Invalid class or character data
    BE --> FE : Validation error; no character created
    FE --> Player : Correct input or choose a valid class
else Persistence fails
    DB --> BE : Transaction rolled back
    BE --> FE : Creation failed; no partial character
    FE --> Player : Offer retry or cancellation
end

note over Player,FE
Class is tied to this character, not to a run.
Character-level class milestones, shared skill-tree choices,
and inventory/items are separate use cases.
end note
@enduml
